From: Yaron Shahrabani <yarons@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: software_isp: Add contrast based continuous autofocus

Cameras of the simple pipeline handler with a focus lens (a VCM listed as
ancillary device of the sensor) stayed at the rest position of the lens.

- The CPU statistics gain a focus measure: the sum of the squared luminance
  differences between neighbouring samples in the horizontal centre.
- The soft IPA interface passes the control info map of the lens to the IPA
  and a lens control list back, as the IPU3 one does; the simple pipeline
  handler applies it with CameraLens::setFocusPosition().
- New algorithm "Af": hill climbing on the contrast with a step that halves,
  then a monitor that searches again when the contrast has changed for some
  time. It does nothing for a camera without lens. Enabled in
  uncalibrated.yaml.

There is no application control yet (AfMode, AfTrigger, LensPosition).
